WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.865
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.865 --> 00:00:05.488
which takes about forty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:08.910
You'll describe the parts of
a check: its catalog entry,

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.799
its function, its rows and outcome,
and its fixtures and tests.

5
00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:15.894
You'll explain the three
severities, Finding,

6
00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:19.238
Warn and Info, and why a
missing value reads as off.

7
00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:24.213
You'll explain why this check is optional
and prefers an export to a live read.

8
00:00:24.213 --> 00:00:29.225
You'll run it on fixtures and on an
export, and see Pass, Fail and Warn.

9
00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:34.012
And you'll explain what the safety tests
refuse, and why a new check inherits them.

10
00:00:34.012 --> 00:00:36.085
Before you start, finish Module 1,

11
00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:40.000
and Microsoft Automation Module
1 for permissions and roles.

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.923
You need PowerShell 7
and Pester 5.5 or later,

13
00:00:42.923 --> 00:00:47.930
and you should be able to read PowerShell
and know Pester's Describe and It.
